{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836524",
      "title": "Collecting User Input with Refs & Forwarded Refs",
      "sourceHash": "45c62f0ff07900ec7c4f0d4aa95216ff2359bad6780148fc315642865b74caf8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.23,
          "end": 3.42,
          "en": "Now that we can see this component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.42,
          "end": 6.57,
          "en": "and enter values here, the next step is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.57,
          "end": 10.32,
          "en": "to collect these values when we click save,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.32,
          "end": 13.23,
          "en": "and to then validate them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.23,
          "end": 16.05,
          "en": "And if invalid values were entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.05,
          "end": 20.22,
          "en": "because at least one of these inputs was left empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.22,
          "end": 23.7,
          "en": "I want to show a little error dialogue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.7,
          "end": 27.48,
          "en": "But if correct values have been entered in all inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.48,
          "end": 29.31,
          "en": "I want to be able to click save",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.31,
          "end": 30.78,
          "en": "and add a new project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.78,
          "end": 33.903,
          "en": "which then should also show up here in the sidebar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.55,
          "end": 38.523,
          "en": "And let's start with this success case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.42,
          "end": 43.353,
          "en": "For this, in this NewProject component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.28,
          "end": 48.24,
          "en": "we need a way of collecting those values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.24,
          "end": 50.613,
          "en": "that were entered into the inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.66,
          "end": 56.34,
          "en": "And one way of course would be to listen to the change event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.34,
          "end": 59.34,
          "en": "and update some state with every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.34,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "and store the entered values like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 64.5,
          "en": "That's one possible approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.5,
          "end": 66.873,
          "en": "about which you learned earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.19,
          "end": 72.57,
          "en": "But here, since I really only wanna read those values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.57,
          "end": 76.71000000000001,
          "en": "when I click this save button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 81.27,
          "en": "I don't want to add and manage all those extra state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.27,
          "end": 85.2,
          "en": "Instead I'll simply use refs, because as you learn,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.2,
          "end": 90.03,
          "en": "you can use refs to connect them to HTML elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.03,
          "end": 94.83,
          "en": "and then interact with those elements, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 94.83,
          "end": 97.32300000000001,
          "en": "to retrieve the value of an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.64,
          "end": 103.64,
          "en": "So for that, we of course must import useRef from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 106.02000000000001,
          "end": 111.02000000000001,
          "en": "And then here I'll have my title ref or just title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 112.41,
          "end": 117.41,
          "en": "however you want to name it, then my description ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 120.39,
          "end": 123.813,
          "en": "And last but not least, the dueDate ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 124.98,
          "end": 129.213,
          "en": "So three refs since I have three inputs down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 130.89,
          "end": 134.61,
          "en": "Now it's important to keep in mind that this input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 134.61,
          "end": 136.47,
          "en": "of course, it's a custom component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 136.47,
          "end": 138.54,
          "en": "It's not the built-in input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 143.54,
          "en": "and therefore adding a ref prop like this might not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 148.17000000000002,
          "en": "depending on the React version you are using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 152.25,
          "en": "If you are using React version 19 or higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 152.25,
          "end": 155.25,
          "en": "this will work and you can simply use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 155.25,
          "end": 159.18,
          "en": "and extract this prop named ref which we added here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 159.18,
          "end": 162.78,
          "en": "in the input component like any other prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 162.78,
          "end": 166.8,
          "en": "just that it will hold a ref as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 166.8,
          "end": 171.6,
          "en": "But if you are using an older version of React, React 18,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 171.6,
          "end": 175.82999999999998,
          "en": "let's say, then this won't work as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 175.82999999999998,
          "end": 179.76,
          "en": "Instead, you'll then have to go to that input component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 179.76,
          "end": 182.4,
          "en": "and there, instead of using this ref prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 182.4,
          "end": 183.9,
          "en": "like a regular prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 183.9,
          "end": 186.21,
          "en": "you have to wrap this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 186.21,
          "end": 188.46,
          "en": "with the forwardRef function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 191.02,
          "en": "that must be imported from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 192.87,
          "end": 196.503,
          "en": "because that will then forward any incoming refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 197.4,
          "end": 202.29,
          "en": "And as you learned, wrap your component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 202.29,
          "end": 203.583,
          "en": "with forwardRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 206.01,
          "end": 209.91,
          "en": "and then store it in a variable or constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 209.91,
          "end": 213.453,
          "en": "which then is exported as a default like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 214.89,
          "end": 218.37,
          "en": "But with that, we're wrapping this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 218.37,
          "end": 220.07999999999998,
          "en": "and this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 220.07999999999998,
          "end": 224.13,
          "en": "therefore now receives that extra parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 224.13,
          "end": 227.73,
          "en": "this second parameter after the props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 227.73,
          "end": 230.853,
          "en": "this ref parameter to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 232.82999999999998,
          "end": 235.59,
          "en": "And with that extra ref parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 235.59,
          "end": 239.16,
          "en": "we can now go to the text area and to the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 239.16,
          "end": 242.28,
          "en": "and there, add this special ref prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 242.28,
          "end": 244.89,
          "en": "which exists on all built-in elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 244.89,
          "end": 249.89,
          "en": "and set it equal to this incoming ref here, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 251.19,
          "end": 252.84,
          "en": "And we do the same on the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 252.84,
          "end": 254.73,
          "en": "because of course either of the two",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 254.73,
          "end": 257.22,
          "en": "is being rendered depending on the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 257.22,
          "end": 258.993,
          "en": "of that text area prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 260.34,
          "end": 261.54,
          "en": "Now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 261.54,
          "end": 265.98,
          "en": "we're able to set this ref prop on our custom component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 265.98,
          "end": 267.45,
          "en": "and it will get forwarded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 267.45,
          "end": 270.33,
          "en": "and can be used inside of that custom component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 270.33,
          "end": 271.743,
          "en": "as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 272.58,
          "end": 277.26,
          "en": "And we can, and should now repeat that for the other inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 277.26,
          "end": 280.2,
          "en": "here for the description input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 280.2,
          "end": 284.613,
          "en": "and then here also for the dueDate input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 285.96,
          "end": 289.53,
          "en": "so that we're setting all these refs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 289.53,
          "end": 291.78,
          "en": "and with those refs being set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 291.78,
          "end": 296.043,
          "en": "we can add a function, handleSave could be the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 297.99,
          "end": 301.65,
          "en": "which should be connected to that save button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 301.65,
          "end": 304.89,
          "en": "So here I'll split this across multiple lines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 304.89,
          "end": 308.22,
          "en": "to make it easier to read and add the onClick prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 308.22,
          "end": 310.3,
          "en": "and point at handleSave here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 312.57,
          "end": 315.84,
          "en": "so that this handleSave function is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 315.84,
          "end": 317.523,
          "en": "when this button here is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 318.51,
          "end": 321.27,
          "en": "Now with that inside of handleSave,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 321.27,
          "end": 324.27,
          "en": "we can get the enteredTitle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 324.27,
          "end": 326.28,
          "en": "by reaching out to this title ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 326.28,
          "end": 328.683,
          "en": "and there the current prop as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 329.94,
          "end": 333.57,
          "en": "you always have to do that when working with refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 333.57,
          "end": 337.35,
          "en": "And then since this will be referring to an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 337.35,
          "end": 338.62,
          "en": "or a text area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 339.48,
          "end": 343.08,
          "en": "and both elements will have a value property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 343.08,
          "end": 346.413,
          "en": "we can access value to get the entered value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 347.97,
          "end": 352.97,
          "en": "And I'll then repeat that here for the entered description",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 353.46,
          "end": 355.863,
          "en": "using my description ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 358.05,
          "end": 360.06,
          "en": "and also repeated of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 360.06,
          "end": 365.06,
          "en": "for the enteredDueDate using this dueDate ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 369.45,
          "end": 373.35,
          "en": "Now we also want to add validation, but we'll do that later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 373.35,
          "end": 377.79,
          "en": "and show that modal if invalid values were entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 377.79,
          "end": 379.62,
          "en": "But for the moment, we'll just assume",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 379.62,
          "end": 381.93,
          "en": "that valid data was entered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 381.93,
          "end": 385.98,
          "en": "and we therefore now need to pass that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 385.98,
          "end": 387.64,
          "en": "back to the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 388.77,
          "end": 392.43,
          "en": "because that's where I'm managing all these projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 392.43,
          "end": 395.40999999999997,
          "en": "and where I want to add this new project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 396.6,
          "end": 399.96,
          "en": "because I will need to then pass it to the sidebar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 399.96,
          "end": 404.07,
          "en": "for example, so we need that state lifted up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 404.07,
          "end": 407.67,
          "en": "to the app component since only the app component has access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 407.67,
          "end": 412.35,
          "en": "to the NewProject component where the data is generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 412.35,
          "end": 415.08299999999997,
          "en": "and the state change will be initiated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 416.1,
          "end": 418.68,
          "en": "and the project sidebar component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 418.68,
          "end": 421.953,
          "en": "where the state data will be needed thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 423.99,
          "end": 426.69,
          "en": "So therefore, here in the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 426.69,
          "end": 429.54,
          "en": "we must add a new function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 429.54,
          "end": 431.19,
          "en": "which I'll name handleAddProject,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 433.95,
          "end": 437.79,
          "en": "here in this function we start this adding process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 437.79,
          "end": 439.593,
          "en": "here, we finish it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 441.93,
          "end": 444.66,
          "en": "And in this function we now of course need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 444.66,
          "end": 449.66,
          "en": "to call setProjectsState again using that function form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 450.45,
          "end": 453.09000000000003,
          "en": "since we're updating the state based on the old state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 453.09000000000003,
          "end": 455.433,
          "en": "so that we don't lose any old state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 457.14,
          "end": 459.72,
          "en": "And we'll return a new object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 459.72,
          "end": 463.59000000000003,
          "en": "where I'll start by spreading all the existing state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 463.59000000000003,
          "end": 465.81,
          "en": "so that the existing data is copied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 465.81,
          "end": 468.033,
          "en": "into this newly returned object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 469.05,
          "end": 472.29,
          "en": "And we then update the project's Array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 472.29,
          "end": 474.33,
          "en": "And I want to update this Array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 474.33,
          "end": 476.733,
          "en": "without losing any old projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 478.05,
          "end": 482.97,
          "en": "Therefore, I'll start by copying all the old projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 482.97,
          "end": 485.793,
          "en": "with the spread operator into this new Array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 486.81,
          "end": 488.88,
          "en": "And then as a last element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 488.88,
          "end": 492.093,
          "en": "we'll add the new project that should be added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
